      ":question/problem": "![](images/7d/7dc7480c7ee27073ff7be7475161742e317b30bf0c3e35af33dc93a772e6034a.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's check our statements.\n\n- The statement \u201c$f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=-1$\u201d is true. The function has a critical point (a corner) at $x=-1.$ In this case,  ${f}^{\u2032}(-1)$ does not exist.\n\n- The statement \u201c$f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=1$\u201d is false. The function has a critical point (a corner) at $x=1.$ In this case,  ${f}^{\u2032}(-1)$ does not exist.\n\n- The statement \u201c$f(x)$ has a local maximum at $x=3$\u201d is false. The function has a local minimum at $x=3$ since $f(3)\\le f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough to $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, select only \u201c$f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=-1$.\u201d"
