      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-47693",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/da/daba5c9c96666b81c5e0e3c0623aa97e234b208dc90f9a3f57785bfcc17552d9.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is plotted above. Given that $f(x)$ is defined on the interval $x\\in [-10,2]$, which points represent the global minimum of $f(x)?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The global extrema of a function are the lowest or highest points of the function's graph over its entire domain.\n\nThe lowest point is the global minimum, whereas the highest point is the global maximum.\n\nAccording to the graph, the lowest point is $A,$ and so this point represents the global minimum of $f(x).$ \n\n**Note:** The point $C$ is not a global minimum, it's a local minimum."
